  {
    "@id": "https://countingcoup.net/event/6562972/761909255/alive-after-5",
    "http://opengraphprotocol.org/schema/title": [
      {
        "@value": "Alive After 5 @ Last Chance Cider Mill - Jul 16, 2026, 5:00PM"
      }
    ],
    "http://opengraphprotocol.org/schema/description": [
      {
        "@value": "Enjoy live music & fun with over 1000 of your closest friends at the first Alive After 5 concert of the summer! 𝙏𝙝𝙚 𝙖𝙣𝙣𝙪𝙖𝙡 𝘼𝙡𝙞𝙫𝙚 𝘼𝙛𝙩𝙚𝙧 5 𝙨𝙚𝙧𝙞𝙚𝙨 𝙞𝙨 𝙥𝙧𝙚𝙨𝙚𝙣𝙩𝙚𝙙 𝙗𝙮 𝘿𝙤𝙬𝙣𝙩𝙤𝙬𝙣 𝘽𝙞𝙡𝙡𝙞𝙣𝙜𝙨 𝙖𝙣𝙙 𝙒𝙚𝙨𝙩𝙚𝙧𝙣 𝙎𝙚𝙘𝙪𝙧𝙞𝙩𝙮 𝘽𝙖𝙣𝙠. The 2026 season of Alive After 5 runs Thursday evenings, 5:00 pm to 8:00 pm, June 11 to July 30, 2026. The outdoor concerts occur weekly at different downtown locations. 𝗩𝗜𝗘𝗪 𝗧𝗛𝗘 𝟮𝟬𝟮𝟲 𝗦𝗘𝗥𝗜𝗘𝗦 𝗟𝗜𝗡𝗘 𝗨𝗣 𝗛𝗘𝗥𝗘: https://downtownbillings.com/the-2026-alive-after-5-summer-concert-series-line-up/ 𝗔𝗗𝗠𝗜𝗦𝗦𝗜𝗢𝗡: Admission is free to the public, however, those 21 and older, wishing to consume alcohol will need to purchase a wristband for $3. 𝗧𝗛𝗘 𝗩.𝗜.𝗣. 𝗘𝗫𝗣𝗘𝗥𝗘𝗜𝗡𝗖𝗘: $10 per person; The tented Western Security Bank V.I.P. Area includes tables, chairs, ice-cold water, and a great view of the stage. V.I.P. Wristbands can be purchased online in advance or in person at the Downtown Billings office at 102 N. 29th Street. Office hours 9:00 am to 4:00 pm, Monday through Thursday, phone (406) 294-5060. 𝘛𝘩𝘦 𝘳𝘦𝘷𝘦𝘯𝘶𝘦 𝘨𝘦𝘯𝘦𝘳𝘢𝘵𝘦𝘥 𝘵𝘩𝘳𝘰𝘶𝘨𝘩 𝘵𝘩𝘦 𝘸𝘳𝘪𝘴𝘵𝘣𝘢𝘯𝘥 𝘴𝘢𝘭𝘦𝘴 𝘢𝘵 𝘦𝘢𝘤𝘩 𝘈𝘭𝘪𝘷𝘦 𝘈𝘧𝘵𝘦𝘳 5 𝘩𝘦𝘭𝘱𝘴 𝘴𝘶𝘴𝘵𝘢𝘪𝘯 𝘵𝘩𝘦 𝘤𝘰𝘰𝘳𝘥𝘪𝘯𝘢𝘵𝘪𝘰𝘯 𝘢𝘯𝘥 𝘧𝘢𝘤𝘪𝘭𝘪𝘵𝘢𝘵𝘪𝘰𝘯 𝘰𝘧 𝘥𝘰𝘸𝘯𝘵𝘰𝘸𝘯 𝘣𝘦𝘢𝘶𝘵𝘪𝘧𝘪𝘤𝘢𝘵𝘪𝘰𝘯 𝘱𝘳𝘰𝘫𝘦𝘤𝘵𝘴, 𝘱𝘶𝘣𝘭𝘪𝘤 𝘢𝘳𝘵 𝘱𝘳𝘰𝘫𝘦𝘤𝘵𝘴, 𝘢𝘯𝘥 𝘰𝘵𝘩𝘦𝘳 𝘤𝘰𝘮𝘮𝘶𝘯𝘪𝘵𝘺-𝘤𝘦𝘯𝘵𝘳𝘪𝘤 𝘋𝘰𝘸𝘯𝘵𝘰𝘸𝘯 𝘉𝘪𝘭𝘭𝘪𝘯𝘨𝘴 𝘚𝘪𝘨𝘯𝘢𝘵𝘶𝘳𝘦 𝘌𝘷𝘦𝘯𝘵𝘴 𝘵𝘩𝘳𝘰𝘶𝘨𝘩𝘰𝘶𝘵 𝘵𝘩𝘦 𝘺𝘦𝘢𝘳. The summer concert series would not be possible without the support of the various host locations and sponsors. 𝗧𝗵𝗲 𝟮𝟬𝟮𝟲 𝗶𝘀 𝗽𝗿𝗲𝘀𝗲𝗻𝘁𝗲𝗱 𝗯𝘆 𝗪𝗲𝘀𝘁𝗲𝗿𝗻 𝗦𝗲𝗰𝘂𝗿𝗶𝘁𝘆 𝗕𝗮𝗻𝗸, and supported by sponsors Hensel Law, Seed of Life Labs, and Desert Mountain Broadcasting Radio group (Planet 106.7,Classic Hits, My 105.9,98.1 KBEAR,94.1 KSKY,910 ESPN,The Zone 96.3)."
      }
    ],
